# Essential Commands

## Frontend (Node.js >= 18.13.0, <= 22.x)

```bash
npm run dev           # Vite dev server + Pyodide fetch (localhost:5173)
npm run dev:5050      # Same on port 5050
npm run build         # Production build (runs pyodide:fetch first)
npm run check         # Type-check with svelte-check
npm run lint          # ESLint + svelte-check + pylint
npm run lint:frontend # ESLint only (auto-fix)
npm run lint:backend  # pylint backend/
npm run format        # Prettier (frontend)
npm run format:backend # Ruff format (backend)
npm run test:frontend # Vitest
npm run i18n:parse    # Re-parse i18n translation keys
```

## Backend (Python >= 3.11, < 3.13)

```bash
open-webui serve --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
uvicorn open_webui.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080 --reload
pytest test/ -k "test_name"
pylint backend/
ruff format . --exclude .venv && ruff check .
```

## Docker

```bash
docker compose up -d
docker compose up -d --build
make install  # same as docker compose up -d
```

## Local dev & builds (developer machine)

Dev iteration runs locally — don't wait on CI/server.

- **Frontend:** `npm run dev` (HMR at :5173) for nearly all theme/branding/UI work. Onboarding/auth pages only fully render with a backend; `:5173` alone shows the "backend required" screen for API-dependent pages.
- **Backend (native, via `uv`):** `uv venv --python 3.12 .venv`; `uv pip install -r backend/requirements.txt` (heavy: torch/chromadb/onnxruntime — one-time, cached in `~/.cache/uv`). Run from `backend/`: `../.venv/bin/uvicorn open_webui.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080 [--reload]`. Set `RAG_EMBEDDING_ENGINE=openai` to skip the embedding-model download at boot; `ENABLE_OLLAMA_API=False` when no Ollama.
- **Local Docker image:** runtime is Colima (`colima start --cpu 6 --memory 12 --disk 80`; buildx linked at `~/.docker/cli-plugins/`). In-build registry network here is flaky (npm/pip `ECONNRESET`) — pre-pull base images and retry, or build the frontend on the host and `COPY` it in.
- **Deploy/release image: CI, not local.** `.github/workflows/build-sakrylle-web.yml` builds **amd64** on push to `theme/sakrylle` → `ghcr.io/ranshen1209/sakrylle-web`; the server (`deploy/docker-compose.sakrylle-web.yml`) only `pull`s. This Mac is arm64 — local builds are arm64 (local testing only); producing amd64 locally needs QEMU (slow).
